{"uncertainty": 0.25, "outcome": "Delivered apb_gpio.v (RTL) and apb_gpio_tb.v (self-checking testbench, N=8 and N=32 instances). The platform's lint, simulation and synthesis checks and the independent review are still pending.", "artifacts": [{"kind": "design_note", "title": "Implementation decisions for apb_gpio RTL", "summary": "The RTL follows [artifact:prj-03bc7b7cf2.microarchitecture.a1]. pready is tied high and access = psel && penable. Decode is is_mapped (word aligned, nothing above bit 5, index at most 8). pslverr = access && (!mapped || (pwrite && index == DATA_IN)). prdata is a multiplexer forced to zero unless the cycle is a mapped read access. Registers are 32 bits wide, masked by a PINS constant. Writes merge under strobes. Status is (status & ~clear) | detected, so a detection beats a clear. irq = |(status & INTR_ENABLE). Reset is synchronous and active low. gpio_in is widened to 32 bits with a generate loop, which avoids a zero-width replication at N=32. Interface behaviour is taken from [artifact:prj-03bc7b7cf2.interface-spec.a1], reviewed per [evidence:prj-03bc7b7cf2.interface-spec.e1] and [evidence:prj-03bc7b7cf2.microarchitecture.e1]. The work serves [requirement:req-837b82982d]. No deviation from either spec is intended."}], "files": [{"path": "apb_gpio.v", "kind": "rtl_source", "title": "apb_gpio RTL", "summary": "APB4 GPIO completer with nine registers, per-pin output and output enable, sampled input, rise/fall/high/low detection, interrupt enable mask, write-1-to-clear status and level irq. Zero wait states; PSLVERR on unmapped addresses and on writes to DATA_IN. Implements [artifact:prj-03bc7b7cf2.microarchitecture.a1] against [artifact:prj-03bc7b7cf2.interface-spec.a1] for [requirement:req-837b82982d].", "entry": "apb_gpio"}, {"path": "apb_gpio_tb.v", "kind": "testbench", "title": "apb_gpio self-checking testbench", "summary": "Directed self-checking bench driving N=8 and N=32 instances. It checks reset values and every read/write register with partial strobes and bits above N. It checks gpio_out/gpio_oe and that DATA_IN is read only. PSLVERR checks cover unaligned, out-of-range and aliasing addresses. Detection checks cover a rising edge that fires once, a one-cycle pulse, a falling edge, both edges on one pin, a level that re-sets after a clear, and low level. Further checks cover partial write-1-to-clear and strobed clears, the interrupt mask, detection beating a clear on the same edge, and reset again. prdata/pslverr must be zero in setup, pready high in access, and the unselected instance must stay quiet. Failures go to $error and passes are counted. It prints the NIRMAAN-SIM verdict before $finish, per [artifact:prj-03bc7b7cf2.interface-spec.a1] section 8 and [artifact:prj-03bc7b7cf2.microarchitecture.a1] section 5.", "entry": "apb_gpio_tb"}], "tool_runs": [], "claims": ["The RTL is written to be Verilator -Wall clean at N 8 and 32 without waivers and latch-free under Yosys; I have not run any tool, so this is unverified.", "The testbench is expected to pass against this RTL under Icarus Verilog (SystemVerilog mode, for $error) and under Verilator with --timing/--binary; not run.", "No formal_spec (SymbiYosys job) is delivered with this task. The interface spec section 8 and microarchitecture section 5 still call for a formal proof at N 8 and 32, so that requirement remains open for a follow-on task."], "escalation": null, "notes": "Testbench timing: pins and bus signals are driven at the falling edge. Each transfer runs setup, then access with checks taken 1 time unit after penable rises, then completion. Consecutive tasks start a new setup immediately after a completion, so transfers are back to back. Detection is checked after two rising edges, as the spec's sample-then-status latency requires. prdata is checked as zero during write access, which follows the microarchitecture's 'forced to zero unless mapped read access'. Both DUT instances share presetn, so each 'reset again' resets both. The bench uses no timescale directive, and neither does the RTL, so the two files are consistent."}
=== FILE: apb_gpio.v ===
// apb_gpio: APB4 GPIO peripheral with edge and level interrupts.
// Implements interface_spec.md following microarchitecture.md:
// zero wait states, no state machine, 32-bit registers masked by PINS.
module apb_gpio #(
  parameter integer ADDR_WIDTH = 8,
  parameter integer N          = 8
) (
  input  wire                  pclk,
  input  wire                  presetn,
  input  wire [ADDR_WIDTH-1:0] paddr,
  input  wire                  psel,
  input  wire                  penable,
  input  wire                  pwrite,
  input  wire [31:0]           pwdata,
  input  wire [3:0]            pstrb,
  output wire [31:0]           prdata,
  output wire                  pready,
  output wire                  pslverr,
  input  wire [N-1:0]          gpio_in,
  output wire [N-1:0]          gpio_out,
  output wire [N-1:0]          gpio_oe,
  output wire                  irq
);

  // Bits 0..N-1 set: pins that exist.
  localparam [31:0] PINS = (N >= 32) ? 32'hFFFF_FFFF : ((32'd1 << N) - 32'd1);

  localparam [3:0] IDX_DATA_OUT    = 4'd0;
  localparam [3:0] IDX_DIR         = 4'd1;
  localparam [3:0] IDX_DATA_IN     = 4'd2;
  localparam [3:0] IDX_INTR_RISE   = 4'd3;
  localparam [3:0] IDX_INTR_FALL   = 4'd4;
  localparam [3:0] IDX_INTR_HIGH   = 4'd5;
  localparam [3:0] IDX_INTR_LOW    = 4'd6;
  localparam [3:0] IDX_INTR_ENABLE = 4'd7;
  localparam [3:0] IDX_INTR_STATUS = 4'd8;

  // ---------------------------------------------------------------------
  // APB decode
  // ---------------------------------------------------------------------
  wire        access = psel & penable;
  wire [3:0]  idx    = paddr[5:2];
  wire        mapped = (paddr[1:0] == 2'b00) &&
                       (paddr[ADDR_WIDTH-1:6] == {(ADDR_WIDTH-6){1'b0}}) &&
                       (idx <= IDX_INTR_STATUS);
  wire        wr_acc = access & pwrite & mapped;
  wire        rd_acc = access & ~pwrite & mapped;
  wire [31:0] wmask  = {{8{pstrb[3]}}, {8{pstrb[2]}}, {8{pstrb[1]}}, {8{pstrb[0]}}} & PINS;

  // ---------------------------------------------------------------------
  // gpio_in widened to 32 bits, zeros above N
  // ---------------------------------------------------------------------
  wire [31:0] in_w;
  genvar g;
  generate
    for (g = 0; g < 32; g = g + 1) begin : g_in
      if (g < N) begin : g_pin
        assign in_w[g] = gpio_in[g];
      end else begin : g_nopin
        assign in_w[g] = 1'b0;
      end
    end
  endgenerate

  // ---------------------------------------------------------------------
  // State
  // ---------------------------------------------------------------------
  reg [31:0] data_out_q;
  reg [31:0] dir_q;
  reg [31:0] in_q;
  reg [31:0] in_prev_q;
  reg [31:0] rise_en_q;
  reg [31:0] fall_en_q;
  reg [31:0] high_en_q;
  reg [31:0] low_en_q;
  reg [31:0] ien_q;
  reg [31:0] status_q;

  // ---------------------------------------------------------------------
  // Next state
  // ---------------------------------------------------------------------
  wire we_data_out = wr_acc && (idx == IDX_DATA_OUT);
  wire we_dir      = wr_acc && (idx == IDX_DIR);
  wire we_rise     = wr_acc && (idx == IDX_INTR_RISE);
  wire we_fall     = wr_acc && (idx == IDX_INTR_FALL);
  wire we_high     = wr_acc && (idx == IDX_INTR_HIGH);
  wire we_low      = wr_acc && (idx == IDX_INTR_LOW);
  wire we_ien      = wr_acc && (idx == IDX_INTR_ENABLE);
  wire we_status   = wr_acc && (idx == IDX_INTR_STATUS);

  wire [31:0] data_out_d = we_data_out ? ((data_out_q & ~wmask) | (pwdata & wmask)) : data_out_q;
  wire [31:0] dir_d      = we_dir      ? ((dir_q      & ~wmask) | (pwdata & wmask)) : dir_q;
  wire [31:0] rise_en_d  = we_rise     ? ((rise_en_q  & ~wmask) | (pwdata & wmask)) : rise_en_q;
  wire [31:0] fall_en_d  = we_fall     ? ((fall_en_q  & ~wmask) | (pwdata & wmask)) : fall_en_q;
  wire [31:0] high_en_d  = we_high     ? ((high_en_q  & ~wmask) | (pwdata & wmask)) : high_en_q;
  wire [31:0] low_en_d   = we_low      ? ((low_en_q   & ~wmask) | (pwdata & wmask)) : low_en_q;
  wire [31:0] ien_d      = we_ien      ? ((ien_q      & ~wmask) | (pwdata & wmask)) : ien_q;

  // Detection from the last sample and the one before it.
  wire [31:0] rise_ev  = in_q & ~in_prev_q;
  wire [31:0] fall_ev  = ~in_q & in_prev_q;
  wire [31:0] detected = ((rise_ev & rise_en_q) | (fall_ev & fall_en_q) |
                          (in_q & high_en_q) | (~in_q & low_en_q)) & PINS;
  wire [31:0] clr      = we_status ? (pwdata & wmask) : 32'd0;
  // OR with detected last: a detection beats a clear.
  wire [31:0] status_d = (status_q & ~clr) | detected;

  // ---------------------------------------------------------------------
  // Registers: synchronous, active-low reset
  // ---------------------------------------------------------------------
  always @(posedge pclk) begin
    if (!presetn) begin
      data_out_q <= 32'd0;
      dir_q      <= 32'd0;
      in_q       <= 32'd0;
      in_prev_q  <= 32'd0;
      rise_en_q  <= 32'd0;
      fall_en_q  <= 32'd0;
      high_en_q  <= 32'd0;
      low_en_q   <= 32'd0;
      ien_q      <= 32'd0;
      status_q   <= 32'd0;
    end else begin
      data_out_q <= data_out_d;
      dir_q      <= dir_d;
      in_q       <= in_w;
      in_prev_q  <= in_q;
      rise_en_q  <= rise_en_d;
      fall_en_q  <= fall_en_d;
      high_en_q  <= high_en_d;
      low_en_q   <= low_en_d;
      ien_q      <= ien_d;
      status_q   <= status_d;
    end
  end

  // ---------------------------------------------------------------------
  // Read data and responses
  // ---------------------------------------------------------------------
  reg [31:0] rdata_mux;
  always @* begin
    case (idx)
      IDX_DATA_OUT:    rdata_mux = data_out_q;
      IDX_DIR:         rdata_mux = dir_q;
      IDX_DATA_IN:     rdata_mux = in_q;
      IDX_INTR_RISE:   rdata_mux = rise_en_q;
      IDX_INTR_FALL:   rdata_mux = fall_en_q;
      IDX_INTR_HIGH:   rdata_mux = high_en_q;
      IDX_INTR_LOW:    rdata_mux = low_en_q;
      IDX_INTR_ENABLE: rdata_mux = ien_q;
      IDX_INTR_STATUS: rdata_mux = status_q;
      default:         rdata_mux = 32'd0;
    endcase
  end

  assign prdata   = rd_acc ? rdata_mux : 32'd0;
  assign pready   = 1'b1;
  assign pslverr  = access & (~mapped | (pwrite & (idx == IDX_DATA_IN)));

  assign gpio_out = data_out_q[N-1:0];
  assign gpio_oe  = dir_q[N-1:0];
  assign irq      = |(status_q & ien_q);

endmodule
=== END FILE ===
